[Music]  abby schudo is tv's perkiest goth a  brilliant scientist and  a shameless caffeine addict we're here  to give you the full story behind  ncis unforgettable forensic scientist  from her trademark pigtails to the  reason her actress departed the show for  good  while abby might be well known for her  cheery disposition  she's also a serious-minded forensics  loving crime solver  this balance feels very natural and it's  no mystery as to why her  actress paulie parrett came to the show  with a degree in criminal justice  she had planned to go into law  enforcement before she got bit by the  acting bug  early roles on shows like the drew carey  show jessie and dawson's creek finally  culminated in 2003 when she landed the  role of abby  abby's first appearance comes in a  two-part story in jag's eighth season  after a body is found near the potomac  river the jag team calls in the  investigative unit at ncis to help them  uncover the truth of this suspicious  death  our introduction to abby is remarkable  to revisit the character debuts nearly  fully formed  while we learn more about her as the  show's many seasons wind on  abby's most distinctive ticks and  trademarks are all on display in her  very first outing but  for a dinner  get me an idea too and i'll make a cafe  atlantico  the first scene featuring abby shows her  calmly watching some guys blast a  mannequin with a shotgun  later when she's detailing some pretty  gruesome x-rays she shares the  particulars of the damage in a detached  almost  board-sounding deadpan that's a  cross-section of what a 12-gauge did to  an l3 to l5  right from the beginning she's unlike  any other character on television  though abby's aesthetic affectations  might lead a viewer to assume she's  gloomy and brooding abby  is actually incredibly upbeat and happy  though she drives an adams family-esque  ford model a  the death investigator is an unusually  bubbly type  he wears three thousand dollar italian  sunglasses and has justin bieber on his  hard drive can't we arrest him for that  perette has said that this perkiness was  very much a choice and  actually modeled after a dog i patterned  everything abby does physically after  this rescue dog that i had named cece  so the way abby stands she stands very  upright and even the way she [ __ ] her  head  everything is done exactly like this dog  abby's energy is all natural too  for the first six years it was hawaiian  punch but then i quit eating and  drinking refined sugar so now i have  unsweetened cranberry juice it tasted  like five  billion percent raw cranberries she  loves extreme music  all black outfits and spooky dolls but  there is one thing she regrets about her  deathly lifestyle  a prominent spiderweb tattoo on her neck  perette doesn't have to reach too deep  to find that feeling in herself  the actress has been open about how much  she hates having the tattoo applied  before filming every day  every day that i come to work i have to  prepare myself for the dreaded putting  on of the neck tattoo  i absolutely hate it perette added that  she tried to get the writers to add a  tattoo removal arc to abby's story but  they wouldn't budge  this is far from the only physical  irritation that perette went through to  play the character  dyeing her hair black once led to a  disastrous allergic reaction  i dyed my hair on wednesday and i went  to work at five in the morning on a  thursday  i would wake up the next morning and my  head was getting bigger and bigger  it would be a real shame if perette was  putting all her actorly effort into a  half-formed character  luckily the writers of ncis have been  able to give abby quite  a full life over 15 seasons abby is the  adopted child of deaf parents therefore  making her proficient in sign language  abby's biological parents are deceased  though the manner in which they passed  is never discussed  born in new orleans the frequent moves  her parents made have given her a wide  breath of knowledge about the southern  united states  her interest in forensics came from one  of the places she lived as a young girl  at one point her family lived next door  to a wrecking yard she found herself  wondering how the cars arriving at the  yard in such a twisted state became so  mangled and eventually learned about the  field of forensics  abby threw herself into her studies  graduating from lsu with full honors and  a bachelor's degree in sociology  criminology and psychology  she then earned her master's from  georgia state in criminology and  forensic science  it is also implied that she got a phd in  chemistry at several points throughout  the series  abby was quickly snatched up by the ncis  team after graduating becoming an  integral part of nearly all their  investigations  abby tends to work alone she has good  reason to be wary of partners though  at one point in the series the ncis team  takes on another forensics expert named  chip sterling  he works as abby's assistant though she  grumbles about the intrusion  the team's senior field agent tony  denozzo jokes about sterling's  relatively minor screw-ups  in time chip launches a plot to frame  tony for murder  apparently holding a grudge against him  from a time before he was on the ncis  team  after this plot is revealed chip tries  to kill abby to avoid being captured  after avoiding her own death abby asks  her director if she can work alone from  that point forward  chip sterling's attack wasn't the last  time someone would make an attempt on  abby schutto's life  a hitman comes after abby in the 15th  season of ncis  her life is only saved by the  intervention of an mi6 agent named  clayton reeves  after tricking the man who wanted her  dead into revealing his identity abby  opts to retire from the ncis  though abby spent 15 seasons with the  team she says her goodbye off-screen  she leaves her bosses a note to let them  know she's gone and heads to the uk  that's where the series claims abby is  to this day  in the real world peret's departure from  the show was a little more complicated  than abby's  abby's goodbye was written as a way  around having to put actor mark harmon  and perette on set at the same time  perette claims that harman  was physically abusive to his co-stars  and that he is the reason  she will never reprise her role on the  series in a revealing social media post  perette made it clear that she's afraid  of harmon  no i am not coming back ever i have  nightmares about it  i have a new show that is safe and happy  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  ncis are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

